WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.674 --> 00:00:02.279
- [Narrator] Country music.
(country music)

00:00:02.279 --> 00:00:04.990
And grabbing your partner for a Do-si-do.

00:00:04.990 --> 00:00:07.616
You probably have a fuzzy
memory of trying to master

00:00:07.616 --> 00:00:10.570
these moves in middle school
gym class, am I right?

00:00:10.570 --> 00:00:12.550
So why were we all forced to couple up

00:00:12.550 --> 00:00:14.399
and endure this embarrassment?

00:00:14.399 --> 00:00:16.695
Well, it's all thanks to Henry Ford.

00:00:16.695 --> 00:00:20.390
- [Man] Now grab your
partner and Do-si-do.

00:00:20.390 --> 00:00:21.855
- [Narrator] He was the father of the car

00:00:21.855 --> 00:00:23.208
and the assembly line.

00:00:23.208 --> 00:00:24.772
But here's a little known fact.

00:00:24.772 --> 00:00:26.467
Henry Ford loved to dance,

00:00:26.467 --> 00:00:28.603
especially with his wife Clara.

00:00:28.603 --> 00:00:30.818
Square dancing has deep
roots in American culture

00:00:30.818 --> 00:00:32.809
dating back to Colonial Times.

00:00:32.809 --> 00:00:34.941
It remained popular
until the waltz and polka

00:00:34.941 --> 00:00:37.450
went mainstream in the 19th century.

00:00:37.450 --> 00:00:40.611
So in the 1920s, Ford took
it upon himself to revive

00:00:40.611 --> 00:00:41.695
the old tradition.

00:00:41.695 --> 00:00:42.591
- [Man] Let's do it y'all.

00:00:42.591 --> 00:00:44.512
- [Narrator] He opened a
ballroom in his hometown

00:00:44.512 --> 00:00:46.869
and encouraged his factory
workers and their families

00:00:46.869 --> 00:00:48.129
to take part.

00:00:48.129 --> 00:00:50.201
He felt square dancing
helped teach manners,

00:00:50.201 --> 00:00:52.587
exercise, values, and grace.

00:00:52.587 --> 00:00:54.709
Soon after, he worked to
create a National Square

00:00:54.709 --> 00:00:56.073
Dancing Program.

00:00:56.073 --> 00:00:58.734
Boards of Education across
the country started endorsing

00:00:58.734 --> 00:01:00.603
Ford's mission, and since then,

00:01:00.603 --> 00:01:02.920
students have been taught to square dance.

00:01:02.920 --> 00:01:05.610
Today, 24, states still
list square dancing

00:01:05.610 --> 00:01:07.784
as their official state dance.

00:01:07.784 --> 00:01:10.527
So if you feel like reliving
awkward gym class moments

00:01:10.527 --> 00:01:12.469
I'm sure you can find
square dancing lessons

00:01:12.469 --> 00:01:13.607
somewhere nearby.

00:01:13.607 --> 00:01:15.360
- [Man] All jump up and never come down.

00:01:15.360 --> 00:01:18.610
Swing your pretty girl ‘round and ‘round.

